'''anabaptistic''' (an″a̤-bap-tis′tik), ''a.'' [< ''Anabaptist'' + ''-ic.''] Of or relating to the Anabaptists or to their doctrines.

'''anabaptistical''' (an″a̤-bap-tis′ti-kal), ''a.'' Same as ''anabaptistic.''

'''anabaptistically''' (an″a̤-bap-tis′ti-kal-i), ''adv.'' In conformity with anabaptistic doctrine or practice.

'''anabaptistry†''' (an-a̤-bap′tis-tri), ''n.'' [< ''Anabaptist'' + ''-ry'' for ''-ery.''] Same as ''anabaptism.''
{{smaller block|''Anabaptistry'' was suppressed in Münster.
{{right|''E. Pagit'', Heresiography, p. 9.}}}}

'''anabaptize''' (an″a̤-bap-tīz′), ''v. t.''; pret. and pp. ''anabaptized'', ppr. ''anabaptizing.'' [< NL. ''anabaptizare'', < Gr. ἀναβαπτίζειν, dip repeatedly, LGr. baptize again, < ἀνά, again, + βαπτίζειν, dip, baptize: see ''baptize.''] To rebaptize; baptize again; rechristen; rename.
{{smaller block|Some called their profound ignorances new lights; they were better ''anabaptized'' into the appellation of extinguishers. {{right|''Whitlock'', Manners of Eng., p. 160.}}}}

